  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1970-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using \\(225=15^2\\) and \\(8=2^3,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} a&=\\frac{\\log_2(15^2)}{\\log_2(2^3)}\\\\ &=\\frac{2\\log_2 15}{3}=\\frac{2b}{3}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(225\\) as \\(15^2\\) and \\(8\\) as \\(2^3\\)",
        "Convert both logarithms to base \\(2\\)"
      ],
